{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q17019280","formula":"C₁₄H₁₄N₂O₂S₂","hill":"C14H14N2O2S2","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":14.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0,"S":2.0},"names":{"en":"2,3-bis(acetylmercaptomethyl)quinoxaline"},"descriptions":{"en":"2,3-Bis(acetylmercaptomethyl)quinoxaline (BAMMQ) is an antiviral agent which inhibits poliovirus RNA synthesis in vitro and in vivo and inhibits human herpesvirus 1 multiplication in vitro. It does not interfere with attachment, penetration or DNA synthesis, but interrupts a late stage in virus assembly and/or maturation. BAMMQ was first identified as an antiviral agent in 1974, when it was shown to inhibit poliovirus growth by 99.8% or more at concentrations as low as 10−5 M. That same year, a patent was filed for BAMMQ and related quinoxaline compounds as antiviral agents, particularly noting their effectiveness against herpes simplex virus."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":188227,"mass":306.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=O)SCC1=NC2=CC=CC=C2N=C1CSC(=O)C","inchikey":"KIYGADXCTZZZDG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"S-[[3-(acetylsulfanylmethyl)quinoxalin-2-yl]methyl] ethanethioate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"188227","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.609,"y":-2.365,"z":-0.771,"el":"S"},{"x":1.609,"y":2.365,"z":0.771,"el":"S"},{"x":3.449,"y":-2.767,"z":1.086,"el":"O"},{"x":3.448,"y":2.768,"z":-1.086,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.399,"y":-1.265,"z":0.575,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.399,"y":1.265,"z":-0.575,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.253,"y":-0.624,"z":0.283,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.253,"y":0.623,"z":-0.283,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.555,"y":-0.641,"z":0.291,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.555,"y":0.64,"z":-0.291,"el":"C"},{"x":1.015,"y":-1.336,"z":0.607,"el":"C"},{"x":1.015,"y":1.336,"z":-0.607,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.772,"y":-1.257,"z":0.571,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.772,"y":1.25